{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba ../../../AGENTS.md | sed -n '145,191p'; nl -ba PAID-BUILD.md; wc -l paid_run.py paid_mutants.py worksheet.py verdict.py plan.json; ls -lt | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"   145\t## 4. Tests\n   146\t\n   147\t- Every test names the requirement or table row it proves; a test that traces to none is deleted, and a retired behaviour's tests leave\n   148\t  with it. The suite stays lean.\n   149\t- Before writing a test, read every function its fixture drives: return shapes, failure classification, the data and attributes it\n   150\t  reads. Check that a name exists before calling it.\n   151\t- Real objects first (real storage on a temporary path, real records). Fake only external services (a model client, a data source, an\n   152\t  HTTP server). Fixture values are realistic (real ISO timestamps, not placeholders).\n   153\t- Tests never reach a paid service or load a credential: `tests/conftest.py` replaces the model and Jev key readers with a refusal, so a\n   154\t  call that escapes its fake transport fails the test.\n   155\t- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A first failure for\n   156\t  any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to fit the code; it changes only when\n   157\t  the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.\n   158\t- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a catch until its\n   159\t  traceback is read. A negative assertion (\"never called\") needs a mutant that makes the call on the tested path.\n   160\t- A check must judge something: it reports how many cases it judged, carries a positive control that fails for the breach it holds, and\n   161\t  fails when its own preconditions fail (exit status, a missing or unidentifiable input). A check over an empty population is\n   162\t  unexercised, not passed.\n   163\t- Tests never depend on the real date or the working directory: pin every date written and read, build paths from the test file's\n   164\t  location, write only inside temporary directories.\n   165\t- Test each entry point as its user calls it (with the defaults the user leaves unset, under the configuration the user runs), not only\n   166\t  the inner function with every argument set.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 5. Verification\n   169\t\n   170\tVerify at the point the change touches, at the sharpest level that shows it works or fails, and stop there:\n   171\t1. Stored data: reproduce the failing case, show the fix flips it, show a mutant of the fix fails the check ($0).\n   172\t2. Only when what the model is asked changed: re-send just the affected calls.\n   173\t3. The touched suites, plus any standing structural checks the change can affect; the full suite once.\n   174\t4. The gate once, at merge (README, \"Build and check\"). The acceptance once, on the final configuration, scored on the frozen ruler\n   175\t   (§7.1). Never a full rerun per fix.\n   176\t\n   177\t- A further check the change does not need is offered in one line, not run. After the checks that prove a change pass, report and close.\n   178\t- To accept a code change, replay stored decisions through the code deterministically ($0); a sampler run proves nothing about code,\n   179\t  and a cached replay proves nothing about the model.\n   180\t- A re-sent request is the bytes production sends, not the archive's canonical JSON: `model.request_identity` sorts keys for the\n   181\t  archive, `model.call` sends the dict as built. Check a harness by comparing an answer's key order with a production answer's.\n   182\t- Before any paid run, `python3 scripts/preflight.py` replays the stored model answers and matching records of the archives and ledgers\n   183\t  it is given through the current code checks and prompts ($0; it skips rows an earlier run refused, so read what it says it skipped)\n   184\t  and prints, per check, the cases judged and the refusals with reasons (it does not yet replay the coverage-start reading's check:\n   185\t  `CURRENT_STATE.md`, open defects). A changed share or a refusal on a case a person would accept is\n   186\t  diagnosed before the run; a paid run is never the way a check or a prompt is first tried.\n   187\t- An acceptance round is a measurement of the final configuration, not a verification step. A new finding in it is recorded with its\n   188\t  census, not answered with another round.\n   189\t- The product runs end to end before anything else is built, and every merge is accepted on the product's own path. A gate passes only\n   190\t  what it runs: name the check that runs a new path, or say that none does.\n   191\t- Measure before claiming. Label estimates as estimates, report every sample, and treat a number in a design document as a measurement\n     1\t# The paid harness, built (PAID-DESIGN.md version 6, D707; for council review before any send)\n     2\t\n     3\tFiles: `paid_run.py` (plan, dry, dry-refused-upstream, send; one sequence per process), `paid_mutants.py` (five mutants of the\n     4\tharness's own checks), `worksheet.py` (the pinned reading worksheet), `verdict.py` (§4's verdict from the read worksheet and the harm\n     5\tfindings, with its checks), `contradictions.py` (the lead parser).\n     6\t\n     7\t## $0 evidence\n     8\t- `plan.json`: the three draws' links (from the probe draws, candidate ids resolved to v14, v16, v21), readers v9, v14 (07-10), v16\n     9\t  (07-15), v21 (07-26) in every draw; the controls retire 247 rows (v14 71, v9 70, v16 56, v21 50), each reader's archive judge rows from\n    10\t  its first retired call on checked equal to its accepted judgements from its link day (no refused first attempt among readers).\n    11\t- `paid-dry-{linked,control}-{1,2,3}.log` (a marker judge for every bought judgement, every answer \"changed\", so propagation is at its\n    12\t  largest): all six complete; links committed exactly the probe draw's (none in controls); every probe link job met; every post-link\n    13\t  reader judgement fresh (call id above the copied archive's top) and every pre-link one from the archive; the upstream snapshot check\n    14\t  run on every linked reader request (267 in linked-1) with no problem; the fixed trajectory (H2) holds (non-reader judgements and every\n    15\t  other table equal to old-2's). Bought: 266 per linked sequence (19 days added by propagation), 247 per control.\n    16\t- `paid-dry-refused-upstream.log`: v14's first attempt on its third judgement refused (an evidence id it was not shown), its retry\n    17\t  accepted; no request shows the refused answer; 267 bought (the retry); snapshot checks clean.\n    18\t- `paid-mutant-{1..5}.log`, each caught: the control not retired (freshness fails); a stale upstream recorded by the harness only\n    19\t  (snapshot problems); v21 missing from the allow-list (the sequence stops on 07-26); a probe link answer missing (stops on 08-06 at the\n    20\t  link job); a non-reader admitted and bought (H2 fails).\n    21\t- `verdict-checks.log`: 14 checks, every one as specified, including round 25's (both gains withdrawn: not improved; one withdrawn alone:\n    22\t  improved; a shared error on a clear date cannot be adjusted) and round 26's (two unquantifiable CPU gains: undecided), round 24's\n    23\t  (5 control definite, 13 linked unresolved: undecided) and the precedence.\n    24\t- `worksheet-dry.log`: the worksheet on the dry stores: 72 distinct pairs per sequence covering the 73 dates (432 rows).\n    25\t- `price.log`: from the dry counts and old-2's archived usage at published rates (cache writes 1.25x): linked about $1.06 each (+10%\n    26\t  prompt growth, +5% retries), controls about $0.91 each; about $5.89 in all; the largest single reservation $0.043, six live at once\n    27\t  about $0.26.\n    28\t\n    29\t## The send (after this review and Alex's ceiling)\n    30\tOne ledger at the ceiling Alex names (`budget_replay.py --init-ledger`), then six processes at once:\n    31\t`paid_run.py send <out> <kind> <draw> <ledger> <ceiling>` for linked-1..3 and control-1..3. Each refuses a ceiling not equal to the\n    32\tledger's, registers its launcher (the stop gate stops all when one dies), holds July's latch, and writes `summary.json`. Then the\n    33\tworksheet, the hand reading (Claude, a blind reader, third reads), the findings file and `verdict.py`.\n    34\t\n    35\tRecommended ceiling to ask Alex: $7 (the estimate plus the live reservations and about 15% margin).\n     357 paid_run.py\n      80 paid_mutants.py\n      69 worksheet.py\n     139 verdict.py\n     140 plan.json\n     785 total\ntotal 5320\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1310 Nov 21 12:09 codex-r28.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 21 12:09 codex-r28.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1112 Nov 21 12:09 round28-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    3414 Nov 21 12:09 PAID-BUILD.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1189 Nov 21 12:09 price.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     254 Nov 21 12:09 worksheet-dry.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     897 Nov 21 12:09 verdict-checks.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    7882 Nov 21 12:09 verdict.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    3636 Nov 21 12:08 worksheet.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     183 Nov 21 12:08 paid-mutant-5.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     200 Nov 21 12:08 paid-mutant-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     183 Nov 21 12:07 paid-mutant-1.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     315 Nov 21 12:01 paid-mutant-4.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     315 Nov 21 12:01 paid-mutant-3.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    4803 Nov 21 12:01 paid_mutants.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   20970 Nov 21 12:00 paid_run.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     736 Nov 21 12:00 paid-dry-refused-upstream.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     808 Nov 21 11:53 paid-dry-linked-3.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     750 Nov 21 11:53 paid-dry-linked-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     692 Nov 21 11:53 paid-dry-linked-1.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     458 Nov 21 11:52 paid-dry-control-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     458 Nov 21 11:52 paid-dry-control-1.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     458 Nov 21 11:52 paid-dry-control-3.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1530 Nov 21 11:45 plan.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   18898 Nov 21 11:42 PAID-DESIGN.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1562 Nov 21 11:42 codex-r27.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   29929 Nov 21 11:42 codex-r27.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     546 Nov 21 11:42 round27-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    2644 Nov 21 11:41 codex-r26.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   26639 Nov 21 11:41 codex-r26.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     872 Nov 21 11:41 round26-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    3761 Nov 21 11:40 codex-r25.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   47474 Nov 21 11:40 codex-r25.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     947 Nov 21 11:39 round25-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    5273 Nov 21 11:38 codex-r24.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   45054 Nov 21 11:38 codex-r24.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1189 Nov 21 11:37 round24-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    6446 Nov 21 11:36 codex-r23.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   82917 Nov 21 11:36 codex-r23.stream\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1134 Nov 21 11:34 round23-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    1847 Nov 21 11:34 parser-validation.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   18027 Nov 21 11:33 parser-validation.txt\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 5 lchingen  staff     160 Nov 21 11:33 __pycache__\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    6312 Nov 21 11:33 contradictions.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
