{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '21,66p;81,112p;122,157p;180,187p'; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '69,102p'; rg -n 'def call\\\\(|return Answer|lookup\\\\(sha' ../../../src/hivemind/model.py; nl -ba ../../../src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '121,135p;154,169p;252,265p;327,357p'\"","aggregated_output":"    21\t## 1. Arms (paired by draw n = 1, 2, 3)\n    22\t\n    23\t- **linked-n:** poc-v120 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive. Its link jobs are answered only by probe draw n's\n    24\t  answers, matched by request hash (`window_test.probe_answers`; any other link job stops the sequence before a purchase), so its links\n    25\t  are probe draw n's proposals, now written. Readers in all three draws: v9 (Data Center FY2027, reads v14), v14 (total revenue FY2027,\n    26\t  reads v8), v16 (total CPU FY2027, reads v14), v21 (revenue growth FY2027, reads v16, and v9 in draws 2 and 3).\n    27\t- **control-n:** poc-v118 from an empty store on its own copy of old-2's archive, its readers' old judgements retired as below.\n    28\t- **Fresh judgements, delimited by date (round 22):** a reader's link is written by an article of day D_R (v9, v14: 07-10, seq 148;\n    29\t  v16: seq 265's day; v21: seq 534's day); its first affected judgement is its first judgement on a day at or after D_R (old-2: seq 167,\n    30\t  274, 542). Every judgement of a reader on a day at or after D_R must be a fresh answer in both arms: in linked-n because its request\n    31\t  carries the dependency block, in control-n because the old request family is retired. The old family of a reader is identified by\n    32\t  reader and judgement day: every archive judge row of that reader (accepted answers, first attempts the stored run refused, and their\n    33\t  retries) whose judgement day is at or after D_R; archive rows carry no day, so a row is assigned to a day through old-2's\n    34\t  `judgements` table (accepted rows) and through its request text (the refused first attempts, whose request equals the retry's before\n    35\t  the correction lines). Every retired row is listed before the send and checked against old-2's judgements by reader and day.\n    36\t- **old-2's stored path:** a labelled historical baseline, outside the fresh-control figures.\n    37\t- All six sequences run at once, one paid call at a time within each (July's latch, round 22), one shared reservation ledger at the\n    38\t  ceiling Alex names.\n    39\t\n    40\t## 2. Harness rules (July's, `dependency-design/july_test.py`, extended to the window)\n    41\t\n    42\t- Harness-only marker, the store lock, never resumed; a stop is final, and its verdict follows §4's precedence (a linked double refusal\n    43\t  fails; an infrastructure stop or a control's double refusal makes the comparison inconclusive).\n    44\t- **Allow-list before the budget transport, per sequence, under July's latch** (admission and the inner call under one lock; the first\n    45\t  refusal closes the sequence): a linked sequence may buy only judge requests of its readers on days at or after their D_R; a control\n    46\t  only the retired readers' judge requests on those days; a link job only from the probe draw. Admission is bound to the replay's\n    47\t  judging day (the harness wraps `round.judge_day` to know the day of every judge request), not to the request's text. Any other request that misses the archive\n    48\t  stops the sequence (round 22 found no legitimate non-reader change on this trajectory). The four answers old-2's own run refused are\n    49\t  given back once each for non-readers, as in the `neither` pass.\n    50\t- Settlement at published rates with cache writes at 1.25x; reservation from request size (D696).\n    51\t\n    52\t## 3. The $0 proofs before the send\n    53\t\n    54\t1. `v120-replay` (done): poc-v120 with each probe draw's own answers meets all 17 link jobs and ends equal to old-2.\n    55\t2. **Linked dry run per draw** (a fake judge answering readers with markers): committed links equal probe draw n's proposals; no link\n    56\t   job outside the probe; no circle correction; every non-reader judgement equal to old-2's by question and day in its request and its\n    57\t   substantive fields (rung, reasons, reference, implied outcome, cites); **freshness checked on the archive side as well as the\n    58\t   transport side** (round 23: a cache hit bypasses the transport): every reader judgement made on a day at or after its D_R has a call\n    59\t   id above the copied archive's top, and none before; **the upstream snapshot:** when each reader prompt is built, the harness records\n    60\t   the judgement id, date, reference and forecast of each question it reads (wrapping `store.current_state` as `judging.build_prompt`\n    61\t   calls it) and checks the rendered dependency block against that snapshot, never against the final ledger; the cases a same-day\n    62\t   upstream update, a carried-forward upstream answer (old-2's v14 has ten judgement days with no v8 judgement that day) and a refused\n    63\t   upstream answer followed by its accepted retry are each exercised; the added days listed.\n    64\t3. **Control dry run per draw:** the retired rows listed and checked; only the retired readers reach the transport, on the right days;\n    65\t   every other judgement equal to old-2's by question and day.\n    66\t4. The stop paths and the latch race, on the window.\n    81\t\n    82\t**Primary line, P, per pair n (round 24: three outcomes):** over all 73 dates, each arm's dates are definite (D), not definite\n    83\t(overlap or clear, N) or unresolved (U), each date keeping its own arm's class even where the other arm is unresolved. Linked-n's\n    84\tdefinite count lies between D_L and D_L + U_L; control-n's between D_C and D_C + U_C.\n    85\t- **Improved:** D_L + U_L < D_C (the least favourable completion still has fewer definite dates in the linked arm).\n    86\t- **Not improved:** D_L >= D_C + U_C (even the most favourable completion cannot give the linked arm fewer).\n    87\t- **Undecided:** otherwise (the unresolved dates could change the result).\n    88\t- **Testable:** D_C >= 2 (known definite dates of the control over all 73, not only dates readable in both arms).\n    89\t- **Readable:** each arm has at least 60 of the 73 dates resolved **in the hand-read classes** (before any credit adjustment): a\n    90\t  coverage policy that deliberately allows at most 13 unreadable dates per arm (82.2%). A readable forecast with unsupported arithmetic\n    91\t  stays readable; its uncertainty reaches P through the credit-adjusted classes the bounds use.\n    92\t- **Credit (rounds 24–25; one rule):** a **gain** is a date on which the linked arm is not definite and the control is definite. Only\n    93\t  gains are ever adjusted; no other date's class changes for credit. When a pair is provisionally improved, **every** gain is reviewed:\n    94\t  both linked answers in force on it (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, are read for July's rule B (arithmetic following\n    95\t  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\n    96\t  rule-B failure on which its reconciliation rests earns no credit (counted definite for P). A gain resting on an unsupported CPU\n    97\t  increment: when the increment can be quantified, the forecast with it removed gives the gain's credit-adjusted class; when it cannot,\n    98\t  the gain counts unresolved: **every** such gain of the pair is marked unresolved, and the bounds are then recomputed once across the\n    99\t  pair (round 26: two gains marked one at a time could each look harmless). Each date keeps its actual class in the report beside its\n   100\t  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\n   101\t  date.\n   102\t- Reported apart, per arm: definite dates that became overlap and those that became clear.\n   103\t\n   104\t**Harm lines (each checked on all three pairs):**\n   105\t- **H1, refusals (round 24):** on **matched reader-days** (a reader judged on that day in both arms of the pair), the attempted reader\n   106\t  judgements and the model refusals among them (first attempts the code refused, terminal refusals included); refusals on linked-only\n   107\t  propagation days reported apart. Harm at **4 or more** refusals above its control on matched reader-days (3 extra is tolerated).\n   108\t  Rationale, frozen before the run: old-2's stored run refused 4 of 1,616 judgements (0.25%), about 0.6 expected per ~250 reader-days, so\n   109\t  4 extra is far above that base rate while up to 3 stays inside ordinary variation. A **linked double refusal** (the corrected answer\n   110\t  refused again: `judgement_refused_twice` stops the day) is a product failure: the verdict is **fail** whatever else holds; a control\n   111\t  double refusal makes the comparison invalid.\n   112\t- **H2, the fixed trajectory:** an unexplained difference in a non-reader request or its substantive output makes the comparison\n   122\t  carried forward) does not have the same specific error.\n   123\t- **H4, the CPU link:** every post-link v14 answer in the linked sequences is read against the exact CPU conclusion it received and\n   124\t  its control's v14 answer that day. Double counting the CPU forecast is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above.\n   125\t- **H5, arithmetic and sourcing (July's rule B):** v9 and v14 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20) in\n   126\t  all six sequences; the unit is a question-date; Claude reads first, a blind reader second; a disagreement goes to a third,\n   127\t  source-backed read whose class decides. H5 is a separate paired harm count: a linked sequence with at least 2 more material failures\n   128\t  than its control is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above (a shared error moves no date).\n   129\t\n   130\t**Verdict precedence:** (1) a **linked double refusal** → fail; (2) **invalid or incomplete** (an infrastructure stop: budget, transport\n   131\tor harness; a control's double refusal; an H2 difference; an arm under 60 resolved dates) → inconclusive; (3) **confirmed harm** (H1, H3,\n   132\tH4 double count, H5) → fail; (4) **untestable** (a control with D_C < 2) → inconclusive, \"the class did not recur\"; (5) **P**: all three\n   133\tpairs improved → pass; any pair not improved → fail; otherwise (some pair undecided) → inconclusive.\n   134\t\n   135\t**The worksheet (pinned before the launch; round 24):** built by `worksheet.py` from the six stores and archives after the run, its\n   136\tformat and code reviewed and run on the dry outputs before the send. One row per distinct v9/v14 answer pair per sequence, keyed by\n   137\tboth judgement ids and the pair's date span; it carries both answers' full `implied_outcome` and reasons, and fields for the reader:\n   138\tthe FY2027 low and high ends as each answer finally states them, the excerpt they come from, the class, a note. H3, H4 and H5 rows carry\n   139\tthe exact request text (dependency block marked), the read judgement each figure came through, and the dated source quotes. Worked\n   140\texample (old-1 09-08): Data Center \"$419 billion for FY2027\" against total revenue \"$414.3 billion ... supports roughly $414–421\n   141\tbillion\": low end 419 is not above high end 421, so **overlap**, though the parser took $414.3B and flagged it definite. Claude reads\n   142\tfirst; a blind reader (Codex, labels shuffled, key kept outside the repository) second; every disagreement that could change a pair's\n   143\toutcome, an H3 or H4 finding, or an H5 mark goes to a third, source-backed read whose class decides. Reading load on old-2's schedule:\n   144\tabout 72 distinct pairs a sequence (up to 438 rows, each read twice: 876 classifications), about 213 linked v14 reviews (twice where\n   145\tan H4 finding is made), 168 H5 marks (84 question-dates twice), the H3 traces, and the full gain review (both supplying answers of every\n   146\tgain, deduplicated), before adjudication; the dry review counts each reader's rows apart; estimated 8–12 hours of reading across the\n   147\treaders, apart from the run's three hours.\n   148\t\n   149\t**Reported beside, not gating:** each link's relation, direction and sign (the weak CPU link disclosed); self-made references\n   150\t(`reference_census.py`'s measures, the `unsourced` scan with the dependency block excluded); v14 linked against control; v21's implied\n   151\ttotal against v9 and v14; linked-only judgement days.\n   152\t\n   153\t## 5. Cost (estimate; the ceiling is Alex's)\n   154\t\n   155\tReader judgements from their links, at published rates from old-2's archived usage: $0.872 a sequence (247 judgements, round 22).\n   156\tLinked sequences: about 19 added judgement days each (round 22's count on the fixed schedule; the dry runs give the exact count) and\n   157\tthe dependency block's prompt growth (about 10%): about $1.05. Three linked and three controls: about $5.8, plus retries and refusals\n   180\tthat pass rule B, the CPU increment shown removed or the pair undecided, H3 triggers on amount, scope or attribution against the\n   181\tcontrol's conclusion in force: §4. The worksheet, its worked example, adjudication for P, H3, H4 and H5, reading time: §4.\n   182\tRound 25: every gain of a provisionally improved pair reviewed, both supplying answers, deduplicated by judgement id; only gains\n   183\tadjusted, by one credit rule; H4 and H5 reach P only through it; H1's boundary stated (harm at 4); reading load counted per reader:\n   184\t§4. The harness review will run two $0 verdict checks: a pair whose control has 2 definite dates and the linked arm none (both gains\n   185\treviewed, withdrawing both gives a tie: not improved); a material error shared by both arms on a clear date (no change to P); the same\n   186\tpair with both gains resting on unquantifiable CPU increments (both marked unresolved together: D_L + U_L = 2, not below D_C = 2:\n   187\tundecided). Round 26: every unquantifiable CPU gain marked unresolved before one recomputation; coverage on the hand-read classes, the\n    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n251:def call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n255:    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n259:        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n286:    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n   121\t\n   122\tdef _indented(text, indent='        '):\n   123\t    \"\"\"A stored value inside a block: every continuation line indented, so no physical line can read as a header or a listed id.\"\"\"\n   124\t    return str(text).replace('\\r\\n', '\\n').replace('\\n', '\\n' + indent)\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n   128\t    \"\"\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\n   129\t    the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\"\"\"\n   130\t    if not state:\n   131\t        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   132\t    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   133\t            f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   134\t            f'    The system\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   135\t            f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   154\t    if deps:\n   155\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   156\t        for d in deps:\n   157\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   158\t            if not target:\n   159\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   160\t                continue\n   161\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   162\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   163\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   164\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   165\t            if full_dependencies:\n   166\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   167\t                continue\n   168\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   169\t    if themes:\n   252\t    return errors\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   256\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   257\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n   258\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\n   259\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\n   260\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   261\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\n   262\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\n   263\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\n   264\t    conn.commit()\n   265\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n   327\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   328\t    done, results = set(), []\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n   353\t            if result['changed']:\n   354\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   355\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   356\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   357\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!*.stream'\"' -g '\"'!*.sqlite'\"' 'scope.*judging|\\\\b1\\\\.058\\\\b|largest single reservation|paid-mutant-5|paid-dry-refused-upstream|worksheet-dry.json' .; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py | sed -n '43,74p;286,325p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '69,84p;131,167p;227,234p;268,290p'; find /private/tmp/claude-501 -path '*linked-1/summary.json' -print | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!*.stream'\"' -g '\"'!*.sqlite'\"' 'scope.*judging|\\\\b1\\\\.058\\\\b|largest single reservation|paid-mutant-5|paid-dry-refused-upstream|worksheet-dry.json' .; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py | sed -n '43,74p;286,325p'; nl -ba ../../../clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '69,84p;131,167p;227,234p;268,290p'; find /private/tmp/claude-501 -path '*linked-1/summary.json' -print | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"./codex-r18.md:28:- **Budget — enough on the observed shapes, completion uncertain.** The existing ledger has **$0.07344613** left. Repricing the three observed job shapes from stored usage, including fresh July jobs and estimated wording growth, gives **about $0.034** for all three draws. The all-SIGN dry shape at the design's stress ratio of 0.37 tokens per byte estimates **$0.0741** in settlements, with a largest single reservation of **$0.00980**. That shape can stop before draw 3 completes. The reservation check protects the approved ceiling. Record a ceiling stop as an incomplete probe with no verdict, and use the existing D700 ledger for all three sequential draws. [Ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/link-census-2026-11-21/ledger.json:2) · [Stress assumption](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:131) · [Reservation check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:131)\n./PAID-BUILD.md:16:- `paid-dry-refused-upstream.log`: v14's first attempt on its third judgement refused (an evidence id it was not shown), its retry\n./PAID-BUILD.md:26:  prompt growth, +5% retries), controls about $0.91 each; about $5.89 in all; the largest single reservation $0.043, six live at once\n./round28-brief.md:3:`paid-dry-refused-upstream.log`, `paid-mutant-*.log`, `verdict-checks.log`, `worksheet-dry.log`, `price.log`). The dry stores are in the\n./price.log:17:   \"estimate\": 1.058\n./price.log:27:   \"estimate\": 1.058\n./price.log:37:   \"estimate\": 1.058\n./price.log:71: \"largest single reservation\": 0.043,\n    43\tdef judged_view(request):\n    44\t    \"\"\"The thesis a judge request is about (its user text begins \"Thesis <id> (\"), or None for any other request.\"\"\"\n    45\t    if 'messages' not in request:\n    46\t        return None\n    47\t    text = request['messages'][-1]['content']\n    48\t    return text.split(' ', 2)[1] if text.startswith('Thesis v') else None\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef is_link_request(request):\n    52\t    questions = request.get('questions') or {}\n    53\t    return bool(questions) and all(qid.startswith(('reads__', 'sign__')) for qid in questions)\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tclass Latch:\n    57\t    \"\"\"One per sequence. Admission and the inner call happen under one lock, so the sequence's paid calls run one at a time: a request\n    58\t    is refused, or is admitted and runs to its end, before the next is looked at. The first refusal closes the latch, and every later\n    59\t    request of the sequence, in any thread, a retry included, is refused before the inner transport.\"\"\"\n    60\t\n    61\t    def __init__(self):\n    62\t        import threading\n    63\t        self.lock, self.reason, self.admitted = threading.Lock(), '', []\n    64\t\n    65\t    def run(self, allowed, refusal, label, call):\n    66\t        with self.lock:\n    67\t            if self.reason:\n    68\t                raise Stop(f'the sequence is stopped ({self.reason}): not sent')\n    69\t            if not allowed:\n    70\t                self.reason = refusal\n    71\t                raise Stop(refusal)\n    72\t            self.admitted.append(label)\n    73\t            return call()\n    74\t\n   286\tdef latch_race():\n   287\t    \"\"\"Worker A is admitted and its call is held open; worker B (an unapproved v8 request) arrives meanwhile; then worker C (v9). B\n   288\t    must wait for A to finish, then be refused and close the latch; C must be refused; only A reaches the inner transport.\"\"\"\n   289\t    import threading\n   290\t    started, release, inner_calls, outcomes = threading.Event(), threading.Event(), [], {}\n   291\t\n   292\t    def inner(provider, request):\n   293\t        inner_calls.append(judged_view(request))\n   294\t        started.set()\n   295\t        release.wait(5)\n   296\t        return {'ok': True}\n   297\t    scope = JudgingScope(inner, Latch())\n   298\t\n   299\t    def worker(name, view_id):\n   300\t        try:\n   301\t            scope('openai', {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': f'Thesis {view_id} (NVDA'}]})\n   302\t            outcomes[name] = 'sent'\n   303\t        except Stop as error:\n   304\t            outcomes[name] = f'refused: {error}'\n   305\t    a = threading.Thread(target=worker, args=('A', 'v9'))\n   306\t    a.start()\n   307\t    started.wait(5)\n   308\t    b = threading.Thread(target=worker, args=('B', 'v8'))\n   309\t    b.start()\n   310\t    b_waited = b.is_alive()\n   311\t    release.set()\n   312\t    a.join(5)\n   313\t    b.join(5)\n   314\t    worker('C', 'v14')\n   315\t    return {'A admitted and finished': outcomes.get('A') == 'sent', 'B waited for A, then was refused': b_waited and outcomes.get('B', '').startswith('refused: unapproved'),\n   316\t            'C refused after the latch closed': outcomes.get('C', '').startswith('refused: the sequence is stopped'), 'only A reached the inner transport': inner_calls == ['v9']}\n   317\t\n   318\t\n   319\tdef dry(scratch, prefix_ledger):\n   320\t    scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   321\t    checks, log = {}, (lambda *a: None)\n   322\t    checks['latch: a request arriving during an admitted call'] = latch_race()\n   323\t    plans = {'control-A': (V118, False, {}), 'control-B': (V118, False, {}),\n   324\t             'linked-A': (V119, True, {('v14', 2): True}), 'linked-B': (V119, True, {('v14', 2): False})}\n   325\t    for name, (cfg_path, linked, changed_on) in plans.items():\n    69\tdef install_stop_gate(ledger):\n    70\t    \"\"\"Process-wide: every `urllib.request.urlopen` call, a helper's internal retry included, first reads the shared ledger. When it is\n    71\t    stopped, or when a registered launcher's lock is free (that launcher died without removing its entry: the gate then stops the\n    72\t    ledger), the call is refused as HTTP 403 (no component retries a 403) and nothing is sent. An attempt whose read came before a stop\n    73\t    was written may finish; one that reads after it is refused. Returns a function that removes the gate.\"\"\"\n    74\t    original = urllib.request.urlopen\n    75\t\n    76\t    def gated(request, *arguments, **keywords):\n    77\t        state = ledger.stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone()\n    78\t        if state.get('stopped'):\n    79\t            raise urllib.error.HTTPError(getattr(request, 'full_url', str(request)), 403,\n    80\t                                         f\"the shared ledger is stopped ({state.get('stop_reason')}): not sent\", {},\n    81\t                                         io.BytesIO(b'{\"error\": {\"type\": \"shared_ledger_stopped\"}}'))\n    82\t        return original(request, *arguments, **keywords)\n    83\t    urllib.request.urlopen = gated\n    84\t\n   131\t    def reserve(self, amount):\n   132\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   133\t            granted = not (state.get('stopped') or state['overrun'] or state['spent'] + state['reserved'] + amount > state['ceiling'])\n   134\t            if granted:\n   135\t                state['reserved'] += amount\n   136\t                state['attempts'] += 1\n   137\t            else:\n   138\t                state['refused'] += 1\n   139\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   140\t                    state['stopped'] = True\n   141\t                    state['stop_reason'] = 'overrun' if state['overrun'] else f'a reservation of ${amount:.6f} would pass the ${state[\"ceiling\"]:.2f} ceiling'\n   142\t        if not granted:\n   143\t            self._note({'refused': amount})                  # after the stop is saved\n   144\t            return False\n   145\t        _LIVE.depth = getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) + 1\n   146\t        return True\n   147\t\n   148\t    @staticmethod\n   149\t    def estimate(request):\n   150\t        \"\"\"The shared reservation of one language-model attempt (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B): `llm_estimate`.\"\"\"\n   151\t        return llm_estimate(request)\n   152\t\n   153\t    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n   154\t        \"\"\"Settle one attempt. A missing, non-finite, zero or negative charge settles at the whole reservation: an answered paid\n   155\t        request never costs nothing, and a failed attempt is charged its reservation. `kind` (llm, jev, embeddings) and the reported\n   156\t        `tokens` go to the attempt line only.\"\"\"\n   157\t        _LIVE.depth = max(0, getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) - 1)\n   158\t        if not isinstance(actual, (int, float)) or isinstance(actual, bool) or not math.isfinite(actual) or actual <= 0:\n   159\t            actual = reserved\n   160\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   161\t            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n   162\t            state['spent'] += actual\n   163\t            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n   164\t                state['overrun'] = True\n   165\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   166\t                    state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, 'overrun'\n   167\t        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants/a-non-reader-bought/linked-1/summary.json\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants/stale-upstream-recorded/linked-1/summary.json\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants/a-probe-link-answer-missing/linked-1/summary.json\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-mutants/a-reader-missing-from-the-allow-list/linked-1/summary.json\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/paid-dry/linked-1/summary.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
