{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The dry runs support the six-arm setup and the expected call counts. The paid entry point can still report success after a design check fails, the worksheet omits the harm evidence, and `verdict.py` can pass incomplete findings. [Dry evidence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:7) · [Paid exit condition](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:325)\n\n### Blocking findings\n\n1. **Use one acceptance gate for dry and paid runs.** The four readers’ cutoff dates and 247 retirements per control check out. But `send` returns success whenever `stopped` is empty, even after a freshness, snapshot, graph, or H2 failure. The dry graph check compares endpoints and sequence numbers while dropping the direction label, and it checks the number of probe jobs rather than the exact jobs consumed. Gate both paths on a completed window, the exact committed graph including labels, exact probe-job consumption, and the freshness and H2 checks. Clear the judging-day scope when `judge_day` exits and verify the request is a judgement before admission. I reproduced a request with only a `Thesis v14` title reaching the inner transport while the day was set. [Retirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:84) · [Admission and day scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:127) · [Dry checks and paid exit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:303)\n2. **Make freshness, upstream provenance, and H2 decisive.** A call ID above the copied archive’s top proves the answer was created sometime in this sequence. It can still be a cache hit on a later day. Tie each accepted judgement to its own dated fresh attempt. The snapshot check searches the whole prompt for the expected values. I swapped the two upstream conclusions in a `v21` fixture and the check passed. Compare each dependency’s rendered block against its own target, judgement date, reference, and forecast, and persist the snapshot for reading. The H2 mutant bought **62** `v8` judgements while its normal summary still said H2 passed. The test caught it only by rerunning a different comparison with a hard-coded reader set. Use the pinned plan independently of admission for H2, and include the omitted typed keys and substantive judgement fields. [Snapshot and freshness checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:154) · [Archive-hit path](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:251) · [H2 comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:210) · [Mutant override](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_mutants.py:50)\n3. **Record and exercise the stop paths.** The missing-reader and missing-probe mutants show their intended refusals. The refused-upstream dry run shows an accepted retry. The supplied evidence does not exercise the paid-path latch race, a refused reservation, or terminal double refusals in both arms. The summary stores a stop string and a list of refused view IDs. It cannot produce H1’s paired reader-day counts or reliably distinguish a linked double refusal, which fails, from infrastructure failure, which is inconclusive. Record dated attempts and typed terminal outcomes, then test those cases through the paid entry point with a fake transport. Include the required preflight on the inputs to be sent. [Required dry proofs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:52) · [Summary fields](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:248) · [Production double-refusal status](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:83) · [Preflight rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:177)\n4. **Finish the worksheet and make the verdict refuse incomplete inputs.** The 432-row dry worksheet demonstrates date carry-forward and the primary forecast fields. It lacks the exact requests, upstream judgement IDs, dated source quotes, and H3–H5 review rows, and it exposes `linked` and `control` labels. The verdict’s arithmetic matches §4 on valid, complete inputs, and all 14 supplied checks passed. Its input handling does not enforce §4. I reproduced a **pass** with 73 off-window date labels and `{}` as the findings file, and another with an invalid credit class. Require the exact calendar, unique sequence-date rows, valid classes, all gain reviews and explicit harm findings. Connect the guard to the six run summaries and exercise the worksheet-to-verdict path on dry artifacts. [Pinned format](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:135) · [Worksheet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:33) · [Verdict input handling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:21)\n\n### Price and ceiling\n\nI independently reproduced **$5.89** from archived usage and the dry call counts, including cache writes and the stated growth and retry assumptions. The largest reservation I found in the marker runs was about **$0.0381**, below the log’s **$0.043** planning figure. Live requests and failed transport attempts can cost more than that estimate assumes. **$7 is a reasonable ceiling to propose after the fixes**, with roughly **$0.85** above estimated spend and six planning reservations. A ceiling stop remains a possible inconclusive outcome. [Price log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/price.log:70) · [Reservation and failed-attempt charging](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:268)"}}
